# Level 9, reached by password WBGR, and the first movie that fires three
# different weapons at two different creatures.
#
# `movies/level9.zmv` was a probe: it held Y and walked a box, and every shot it
# ever fired carried `$5C`. That is why the coverage table listed eight of
# `enemy_d301_collide`'s branches and five of `enemy_cdde_collide`'s as untaken
# -- neither creature had ever been hit by anything but the default gun, and
# neither of them takes damage from it.
#
# What the per-level weapon table said (docs/cosim.md) is that level 9's own
# object list holds three: type `$00` at (1150,650) is `$5C`, type `$02` at
# (260,252) is `$5D` -- the ice weapon, and `CDDE_HIT_DAMAGE` -- and the two
# type `$06` objects are `$5F`, which is the one id in reach that hurts
# `$81:D301`. This movie collects the second and the third and spends them.
#
# The route is walked against walls rather than against the router. Level 9's
# corridors are narrow and its actors get in the way, so a leg timed to end in
# open ground ends somewhere different on a slower pass; every turn here is
# taken *at* a wall, where holding the button longer changes nothing. The one
# exception is the descent to the ice weapon, which is timed, and the one
# back-off that finds the vertical corridor at x=348: walk east into the wall at
# x=392, hold Left for exactly twenty frames, then go up.
#
# Phases:
#   2700  walk west and north to the ice weapon at (260,252), 99 shots
#   3730  back east, up, west and down to the $81:D301 creature at (107,315)
#   4270  fire ice at it            -> d301_special, and the whole freeze family
#   4510  B, then fire $5C at it    -> d301_shot_immune
#   4830  north-west to the $06 object at (43,69), 300 shots of $5F
#   5650  return to the same spot and fire $5F
#                                   -> d301_died, d301_survived, d301_reseed,
#                                      d301_no_reseed
#   6430  B twice, back to the ice  (B is only read every other pass: presses
#         closer together than about forty frames are dropped, which is why the
#         two are sixty apart)
#   6520  south and east to the $81:CDDE ground, arriving at (934,673)
#   7280  60-frame legs with Y held -> cdde_survived, cdde_react_begin
#
# `cdde_killed_reacting` is still untaken and this movie says why: `$81:CC90`
# arms the countdown at 4, and the flash lasts 30 frames and puts it back up to
# 20 -- so finishing one *during* the flash is 21 hits in 30 frames, against a
# fire rate of one shot every eight frames and about four hits a shot.
#
